AB  - This paper introduces BIM2RDT (Building Information Models to Robot-Ready Construction Digital Twins), an AI-assisted pipeline transforming static BIM into dynamic digital twins for construction robot navigation and safety monitoring. The framework fuses BIM geometry, unmanned ground vehicle (UGV) visual observations, and IoT sensor data to enable automated site monitoring and safety-aware path planning. A core contribution is Semantic-Gravity ICP (SG-ICP), a point cloud registration method leveraging LLM-guided semantic reasoning to assign BIM-family-specific upright priors, improving alignment robustness in low-feature construction scenes. The framework integrates YOLOE open-vocabulary detection for BIM-conditioned perception and demonstrates safety monitoring through Hand-Arm Vibration (HAV) sensing written into IFC-compatible digital twin representations. Controlled experiments show SG-ICP reduces RMSE by approximately 60%–97% over standard registration methods in high-noise scenarios. These capabilities represent an initial step towards agentic construction workflows, with LLM-orchestrated pipelines that condition perception, trigger IFC updates, and propose navigation constraints. © 2026 Published by Elsevier B.V.
