UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010850218?origin=resultslist
AD  - Department of Geotechnical Engineering, Tongji University, Shanghai, 200092, China
AB  - Geological uncertainty ahead of the tunnel face presents significant challenges to the safety and efficiency of tunnel construction. To address this issue, this paper explores the feasibility of using a digital twin approach to enhance geological modeling and rock classification. The proposed method integrates multi-source geological data to construct a multi-dimensional geological virtual model, and applies a fuzzy cloud probability model to quantify uncertainty, enabling intelligent classification of surrounding rock. Results from tests on five rock tunnel projects using the iS3 platform show that the overall rock classification accuracy of the method is 92.95 %. These findings clearly demonstrate that the digital twin approach significantly improves geological transparency, risk management, and decision-making efficiency in complex rock tunnel environments. Future research will focus on exploring the application of this method in soft soils, underwater tunnels, and other broader geological conditions. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.
