AB  - Shield attitude control is vital for tunnel safety, yet existing single-scene models lack generalization and real-time adaptability across diverse geologies. Herein, a digital twin (DT)-driven intelligent control framework integrating the improved black kite algorithm (IBKA), natural gradient boosting (NGBoost), and NSGA-III is proposed to achieve automated, optimal attitude management. Using a Wuhan metro underpass as a case study, the framework’s performance was validated across typical geological conditions. Key results demonstrate that (1) the IBKA-NGBoost prediction model achieves an optimal accuracy-efficiency trade-off for small-sample data under two geological conditions, with R2values exceeding 0.91 for seven attitude indicators and a training time of only 29.2 s; (2) the integrated IBKA-NGBoost-NSGA-III framework enables adaptive multiscenario optimization, reducing deviations of the seven attitude parameters by an average of 69.3%; adjustment of the 12 key construction variables yielded a maximum improvement of 84.8%; and (3) embedding this algorithm into a DT system enhanced real-time regulatory capability, supporting adaptive adjustment for improved construction guidance and safety. Consequently, the proposed method enables adaptive adjustment, thereby supporting construction guidance and safety management. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd.
