AB  - Intelligent agent assistants are becoming essential for efficient interaction in safety monitoring digital twin (DT) systems. However, their deployment in small- and medium-scale hydropower projects remains limited by complex modules, inefficient interaction, and constrained computing resources. To bridge this gap, this paper proposes a lightweight agent assistant for DT systems that integrates graph retrieval-augmented generation (GraphRAG)-enabled task-oriented context construction with Gemma-based large language model (LLM) response generation. Graph-constrained automatic speech recognition (ASR) correction improves intent recognition and hands-free operation. Additionally, a conflict resolution and dynamic update strategy supports lightweight knowledge graph (KG) maintenance. Ultimately, field validation in a practical medium-scale hydropower project DT system demonstrates that the agent assistant reduces users' operational cognitive load and ensures response accuracy. As a result, this paper provides a lightweight, low-cost, and portable DT interaction solution for safety monitoring and intelligent management in resource-constrained hydropower projects, while supporting human-machine collaboration in DT systems. © 2026 Elsevier B.V. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
